        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Language and gender"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.5,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 289,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Gender awareness and vocabulary"
      },
      {
        "y": 88.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 520.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "In professional contexts and elsewhere, we often take care to use gender-neutral language in English."
      },
      {
        "y": 100.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 421.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "David Crystal, in The Cambridge Encyclopedia of the English Language, writes:"
      },
      {
        "y": 125.1,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 485.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Attention has been focused on the replacement of ‘male’ words with a generic meaning by"
      },
      {
        "y": 137.1,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 484.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "neutral items – chairman, for example, becoming chair or chairperson (though not without"
      },
      {
        "y": 149.1,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 496.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "controversy) or salesman becoming sales assistant. In certain cases, such as job descriptions,"
      },
      {
        "y": 161.1,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 480.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the use of sexually neutral language has become a legal requirement. There is continuing"
      },
      {
        "y": 173.1,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 491.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "debate between extremists and moderates as to how far such revisions should go – whether"
      },
      {
        "y": 185.1,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 476.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "they should affect traditional idioms such as man in the street1 and Neanderthal Man2, or"
      },
      {
        "y": 197.1,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 472,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "apply to parts of words where the male meaning of man is no longer dominant, such as"
      },
      {
        "y": 209.1,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 507.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "manhandle3 and woman. The vocabulary of marital status has also been affected, notably in the"
      },
      {
        "y": 221.1,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 344.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "introduction of Ms as a neutral alternative to Miss or Mrs."
      },
      {
        "y": 246.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 518.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1a typical person (could be replaced by person in the street) 2a now-extinct species that were the ancestors of"
      },
      {
        "y": 258.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 295.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "present-day humans 3handle roughly, using force"
      },
      {
        "y": 273.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 381.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Here are some examples of gender-neutral variations of vocabulary."
      },
      {
        "y": 291.7,
        "x0": 105.1,
        "x1": 362.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "older usage current usage"
      },
