      {
        "y": 68.6,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "99.1"
      },
      {
        "y": 71.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 329.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Answer these questions about the text opposite."
      },
      {
        "y": 87.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 515.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 Why do you think there have been attempts to introduce gender-neutral language of the kind"
      },
      {
        "y": 99.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 242.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "described by David Crystal?"
      },
      {
        "y": 111.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 451.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 How would you explain this expression: ‘male’ words with a generic meaning?"
      },
      {
        "y": 123.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 474.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 Why do you think there might have been controversy about attempts to change the"
      },
      {
        "y": 135.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 194.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "word chairman?"
      },
      {
        "y": 147.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 483.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 What do more extreme advocates of making English gender-neutral want to do that is"
      },
      {
        "y": 159.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 261.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "unacceptable to the moderates?"
      },
      {
        "y": 171.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 312.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 Why was Ms introduced and why is it useful?"
      },
      {
        "y": 187.9,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "99.2"
      },
      {
        "y": 190.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 354.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Change these sentences so they reflect modern usage."
      },
      {
        "y": 207.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 417.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 Three firemen helped put out a fire at a disused warehouse last night."
      },
      {
        "y": 219.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 447.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 A spokesman for the Department of Education provided us with a statement."
      },
      {
        "y": 231.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 326.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 Cleaning lady wanted for house in Priory Street."
      },
      {
        "y": 243.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 403.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 The helpline is continuously manned even during holiday periods."
      },
      {
        "y": 255.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 367.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 All our air hostesses are fluent in at least three languages."
      },
      {
        "y": 267.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 300.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 The fibres in this garment are man-made."
      },
      {
        "y": 279.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 374.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "7 Policemen today spend more time in cars than on the beat."
      },
      {
        "y": 291.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 270.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "8 This was a great step for mankind."
      },
      {
        "y": 303.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 341.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "9 The man in the street has little time for such issues."
      },
      {
        "y": 315.2,
        "x0": 110.2,
        "x1": 377.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "10 Salesmen are often well trained and can be very persuasive."
      },
      {
        "y": 331.2,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "99.3"
      },
      {
        "y": 333.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 346.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Choose the correct word to complete each sentence."
      },
      {
        "y": 350.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 340.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 She always dresses in a very feminine / female way."
      },
      {
        "y": 362.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 366.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 The masculine / male cat is less aggressive than his sister."
      },
      {
        "y": 374.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 327.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 Do you girlfriends / guys fancy meeting up later?"
      },
      {
        "y": 386.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 332.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 The bar was full of loud, lad / laddish young men."
      },
      {
        "y": 398.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 356.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 Ross likes to see himself as a tough male / macho man!"
      },
      {
        "y": 410.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 405.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 Anna’s going away for the weekend with a few girlfriends / females."
      },
      {
        "y": 426.6,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "99.4"
      },
      {
        "y": 429.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 223.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Answer these questions."
      },
      {
        "y": 445.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 527.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 Do you think that using gender-specific language affects people’s attitudes to men and women’s"
      },
      {
        "y": 457.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 194.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "roles in society?"
      },
      {
        "y": 469.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 517,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 Does your language ever use male words generically? If so, give examples of words you use to"
      },
      {
        "y": 481.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 239.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "avoid gender stereotyping."
      },
      {
        "y": 493.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 506.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 How do you feel about imposing language changes of the different kinds that David Crystal"
      },
      {
        "y": 505.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 171.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "describes?"
      },
      {
        "y": 517.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 514.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 Do terms of address (i.e. Mr, Mrs, etc.) in your language indicate whether people are married?"
      },
      {
        "y": 529.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 455.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 Do you think it is better if terms of address indicate marital status or not? Why?"
      },
      {
        "y": 541.8,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 532.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 A grammatical problem in this area is the use of he/his to refer to a person of either gender. In the"
      },
      {
        "y": 553.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 526.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "sentence ‘A government minister may have to neglect his family’, the minister could be a man or"
      },
      {
        "y": 565.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 519.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "a woman. However, the use of ‘his’ assumes, perhaps wrongly, that it is a man. How could you"
      },
      {
        "y": 577.8,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 310.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "rewrite this sentence to avoid this problem?"
      }
